{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "82a4c2c0-019d-44da-9116-560c1ffeade3",
    "name": "CatalogMuse agents",
    "description": "HTTP contract for the Go backend. The service listens on 127.0.0.1:8790. Create a job, watch it, then approve the waiting step. The copywriter and the auditor stop once, together. A change note sends the listing back to the copywriter, and the auditor runs again before that same approval. Nothing here publishes a listing. The supplier photo is raw base64, not a data URL, and must decode to under 8 MB. marketplaces is amazon, walmart, or both. Omit it for Amazon only. Walmart is a separate title, an HTML key-feature list, and a shelf description. The auditor checks each selected marketplace in code, and approve stays closed until every list is clear. Image urls are presigned GETs for asinzen-catalogmuse. They last 12 hours and are signed again on each Get job. Without a bucket, url is this service's file route.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
